          "message": {
            "text": "The public route accepts any syntactically valid 32-36 character UUID and does not apply check_rate_limit or a server-side cache. Every request creates a new async HTTP client and can wait up to eight seconds while trying two external image services with redirects enabled. An attacker can submit many distinct UUIDs to create outbound connections and hold request resources even when no image exists."
